### Testing

- Put unit tests beside their code in `#[cfg(test)] mod tests`; put tests of the public API under `tests/`.
- Name a test for the behavior it proves (`rejects_empty_input`), and assert on `Result`/`Option` values with a pattern match, not `.unwrap()` on the tested path.
- Reserve `#[should_panic]` for a genuine panic contract; never use it to paper over an untested `Result` path.
<!-- Project-specific / Rust-Testing -->

### Common Mistakes

- Borrow-silencing clone: `.clone()` reached for to quiet a borrow-checker error => restructure ownership or borrow instead.
- String error: an error carried as a `String`, leaving callers only a text match => return a typed error enum.
- Shared-ownership web: an `Rc<RefCell<_>>` or `Arc<Mutex<_>>` threaded through modules that do not otherwise share state => give the state one owner and pass messages or borrows.
- Unjustified `unsafe`: an `unsafe` block with no `// SAFETY:` comment => name the invariant that makes it sound, or remove the `unsafe`.
- Speculative trait: a trait with every method `pub` and only one implementation, built "just in case" => use the concrete type until a second implementation exists.
<!-- Project-specific / Rust-Common Mistakes -->
